{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39836324",
      "title": "Setting Timers & Managing State",
      "sourceHash": "e5a226122ffe623ca686071507c77439cd8536fb1b1bbacb9fd23b9cca449708",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.69,
          "end": 3.18,
          "en": "So let's now make sure that we start a timer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.18,
          "end": 7.17,
          "en": "when this start challenge button is pressed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.17,
          "end": 9.69,
          "en": "and for that, of course, we'll need a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.69,
          "end": 13.2,
          "en": "handleStart, sounds like a fitting name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.2,
          "end": 15.28,
          "en": "where we wanna set a timer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.38,
          "end": 19.95,
          "en": "and a timer can be set in JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.95,
          "end": 23.043,
          "en": "by using the built-in setTimeout function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.91,
          "end": 28.89,
          "en": "This allows us to set a timer, maybe, of 1,000 milliseconds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.89,
          "end": 32.07,
          "en": "for example, that will execute this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.07,
          "end": 33.513,
          "en": "once it expired.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.68,
          "end": 38.553,
          "en": "So that's built into JavaScript, not React specific.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.66,
          "end": 42.78,
          "en": "Now, of course, the time here which has to be specified",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.78,
          "end": 46.353,
          "en": "in milliseconds should be based on this target time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 47.37,
          "end": 49.26,
          "en": "but target time is in seconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.26,
          "end": 53.2,
          "en": "So we have to multiply it with 1,000 to get milliseconds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 54.75,
          "end": 56.97,
          "en": "and then we'll need some state to know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.97,
          "end": 58.653,
          "en": "once the timer expired.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.82,
          "end": 62.7,
          "en": "For that, I'll of course use the useState hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.7,
          "end": 64.48,
          "en": "which is imported from React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 65.55,
          "end": 67.5,
          "en": "and initially, that's false, let's say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.5,
          "end": 69.733,
          "en": "because I'll name it timerExpired",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.25,
          "end": 75.99,
          "en": "and we have a setTimerExpired state updating function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 75.99,
          "end": 79.77,
          "en": "let's say, and of course, the goal is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 79.77,
          "end": 83.92,
          "en": "inside of this timeout function, to setTimerExpired to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 87.87,
          "end": 90.09,
          "en": "So if we reach this line of code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 90.09,
          "end": 92.1,
          "en": "if this function gets executed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 92.1,
          "end": 96.15,
          "en": "the player basically lost because the timer expired",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 96.15,
          "end": 98.523,
          "en": "before it was stopped by the player.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 99.57,
          "end": 101.97,
          "en": "So we can now use this state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 101.97,
          "end": 106.56,
          "en": "to, for example, conditionally output a paragraph here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 106.56,
          "end": 109.28999999999999,
          "en": "where we check if timerExpired is true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 109.28999999999999,
          "end": 111.78,
          "en": "and if that's the case, we output a paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 111.78,
          "end": 113.547,
          "en": "where we say \"You lost\".",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 115.71000000000001,
          "end": 118.08,
          "en": "This is not the final solution I want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 118.08,
          "end": 120.48,
          "en": "but it's good enough for now to get an idea",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 120.48,
          "end": 122.853,
          "en": "of whether the game's over or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 124.44,
          "end": 127.26,
          "en": "Now, of course, handleStart now also must be connected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 127.26,
          "end": 128.85,
          "en": "to this button here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 128.85,
          "end": 133.503,
          "en": "Here, on click, we want to execute handleStart like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 135.78,
          "end": 139.143,
          "en": "Now, if we save that and reload, if I click this button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 139.98,
          "end": 144.39,
          "en": "nothing changes, but after one second, I see \"You lost\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 144.39,
          "end": 145.86,
          "en": "and at the moment, there's of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 145.86,
          "end": 147.603,
          "en": "nothing we can do about that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 149.572,
          "end": 153.44,
          "en": "Therefore, we can also add a second piece of state here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 154.44,
          "end": 156.303,
          "en": "which initially also is false,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 157.2,
          "end": 161.1,
          "en": "where we store whether the timer has been started.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 161.1,
          "end": 165.4,
          "en": "So timerStarted could be the name and setTimerStarted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 168.12,
          "end": 171.75,
          "en": "and we want to set this to true right before we set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 171.75,
          "end": 174.51,
          "en": "the timer, not inside of it once it expired,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 174.51,
          "end": 178.62,
          "en": "but right before it, setTimerStarted to true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 181.05,
          "end": 182.1,
          "en": "or right after it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 182.1,
          "end": 185.73,
          "en": "That also works because this line will execute immediately",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 185.73,
          "end": 189.45,
          "en": "after setting the timer, not after it expired.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 189.45,
          "end": 192.45,
          "en": "It's only the code in here that will only execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 192.45,
          "end": 193.893,
          "en": "once the timer expired.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 194.73,
          "end": 198.52,
          "en": "This code here will execute right after the timer was set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 200.19,
          "end": 202.92000000000002,
          "en": "and with this second state added here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 202.92000000000002,
          "end": 206.97,
          "en": "we can now also update the UI to reflect this information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 206.97,
          "end": 208.353,
          "en": "that the timer is running.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 209.52,
          "end": 211.777,
          "en": "For example, here, instead of always saying",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 211.777,
          "end": 216.37,
          "en": "\"Start Challenge\", we can check if timerStarted is truthy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 217.29,
          "end": 220.02,
          "en": "and if that's the case, we wanna show \"Stop\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 220.02,
          "end": 221.97,
          "en": "instead of start.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 221.97,
          "end": 222.813,
          "en": "Like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 225.45,
          "end": 229.95,
          "en": "Here, I want to add the active CSS class conditionally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 229.95,
          "end": 232.53,
          "en": "So we can check if timerStarted is truthy,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 232.53,
          "end": 235.02,
          "en": "in which case we add active as a class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 235.02,
          "end": 236.523,
          "en": "otherwise, we add nothing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 238.8,
          "end": 241,
          "en": "So we set the class name to undefined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 242.04,
          "end": 245.867,
          "en": "and then in here, we check if timerStarted is true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 247.5,
          "end": 250.767,
          "en": "and if that's the case, I wanna output \"Time is running\".",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 251.94,
          "end": 256.15,
          "en": "Otherwise, I want to output \"Timer inactive\" like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 258.18,
          "end": 261.66,
          "en": "so that the UI is updated based on whether the timer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 261.66,
          "end": 263.013,
          "en": "is running or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 264.9,
          "end": 267.93,
          "en": "So with that, if we save this, if I click \"Start Challenge\",",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 267.93,
          "end": 271.77,
          "en": "the UI updates, but I of course still have no way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 271.77,
          "end": 273.67,
          "en": "of stopping this challenge",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 274.92,
          "end": 277.62,
          "en": "and therefore, we'll also need another function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 277.62,
          "end": 280.293,
          "en": "handleStop, sounds like a fitting name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 281.19,
          "end": 284.77,
          "en": "where I, in the end, want to stop this timer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 285.81,
          "end": 289.53,
          "en": "and the question there for now is how do we get access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 289.53,
          "end": 292.11,
          "en": "to this timer in this function here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 292.11,
          "end": 294.873,
          "en": "And that's where a ref can help us.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}